{title: Proclaim Liberty}
{subtitle: Leviticus 25:1–55}
{key: D}
{tempo: 84}
{time: 2/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [D] | ×14

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
The Lord spoke to [Bm]Moses [G]on Mount Sinai,
Speak to the people [D]of Israel's [G]line.
When you enter the land [Bm]I [G]give to you,
The land itself must [A]keep [D]the Sabbath true.
Six years sow the [Bm]field [G]and prune the vine,
Gather the produce [D]in its [G]season's time.
But in the seventh year [Bm]let it [G]rest,
A Sabbath of complete and [A]holy rest.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[G]On the [D]tenth day [A]sound the [Bm]ram's horn [G]loud,
Proclaim [D]liber[A]ty throughout the [G]crowd.
Return to [D]proper[F#7/A#]ty and [Bm]family's [G]door,
The fiftieth year opens up [D]once more.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Do not take advantage of neighbor's [Bm]need,
[G]Fear the Lord and keep His holy [D]creed.
The [G]land is mine and you are tenants [Bm]here,
Re[G]deem the property and draw [A]near.
[D]If a brother sells himself to [Bm]you,
[G]He is not a slave to do as [D]you.
[G]Treat him as a hired worker [Bm]found,
Un[G]til the Jubilee year is [A]found.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
On the [G]tenth day [D]sound the [A]ram's horn [Bm]loud,
Pro[G]claim liber[D]ty through[A]out the crowd.
Re[G]turn to proper[D]ty and [F#7/A#]family's [Bm]door,
The [G]fiftieth year [A]opens up once [D]more.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
They are my servants from Egypt [Bm]brought,
[G]Not to be sold as slaves are [D]caught.
Do not rule [G]over them with harsh com[Bm]mand,
[G]Fear the God who gives you all the [A]land.
[D]Help the poor to live among the [Bm]rest,
[G]Do not charge interest on your [D]chest.
[G]I am the Lord who brought you [Bm]out,
To [G]give you Canaan as your [A]fruit.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
On the [G]tenth day [D]sound the [A]ram's horn [Bm]loud,
Pro[G]claim liber[D]ty through[A]out the crowd.
Re[G]turn to proper[D]ty and [F#7/A#]family's [Bm]door,
The [G]fiftieth year opens up once [D]more.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
The land will yield its fruit for [Bm]three,
[G]Eat from the old crop with such [D]glee.
Se[G]curely live in the land you [Bm]hold,
[G]Faithful to the story God has [A]told.
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
Pro[G]claim liber[D]ty through[F#7/A#]out the [Bm]land,
[G]In the hands of the Lord's own [D]hand.
{end_of_verse}
